# 16. Important banking security requirements

For a real banking app, you should also implement:

- OAuth2/OIDC instead of raw username/password handling where possible
- Short-lived access tokens and secure refresh flow
- Device binding / risk-based authentication
- Root/jailbreak detection strategy
- Play Integrity API / device attestation
- TLS hardening and cert pin rotation
- Fraud detection hooks
- Secure session timeout and re-authentication
- Anti-overlay / anti-tampering protections
- No sensitive data in logs, screenshots, clipboard, or notifications
- Server-side authorization for every action
- Strong transfer approval flows
- Accessibility-safe but secure UX
- Full audit logging on backend
- Regulatory compliance: PCI DSS, GDPR, PSD2, FFIEC, etc. depending on region

