# Important security note
This example is only a UI/data skeleton. It is not suitable for a real banking app as-is.

For a production banking application, you must also implement:

- real backend authentication with short-lived tokens
- certificate pinning
- encrypted local storage
- biometric re-auth for sensitive actions
- device integrity checks
- fraud/risk monitoring
- secure session timeout
- root/jailbreak/emulator detection strategy
- audit logging
- PCI/financial regulatory compliance
- server-side authorization for every transaction
- no hardcoded credentials
- no client-side trust of balances or transfers

## Things you should never do in a real banking app
- store plaintext passwords
- validate money transfers only on-device
- hardcode API secrets in the APK
- trust client-calculated balances
- expose detailed errors during auth
- skip TLS hardening

