# 12) Important security requirements for a real banking app

A real banking application should also include:

- Backend-driven authentication, not hardcoded auth logic
- MFA / OTP / device binding
- Short-lived access tokens and secure refresh flow
- Session timeout and re-authentication
- Fraud/risk signals
- TLS-only networking
- Real certificate pin rotation strategy
- Root/jailbreak detection
- Emulator/debugger detection where appropriate
- Screenshot blocking for sensitive screens:
  ```kotlin
  window.setFlags(
      WindowManager.LayoutParams.FLAG_SECURE,
      WindowManager.LayoutParams.FLAG_SECURE
  )
  ```
- No sensitive data in logs
- No account numbers except masked values
- PCI DSS / GDPR / local regulatory compliance
- Accessibility and secure UX review
- Tamper protection and integrity checks
- Proper server-side authorization for every account and transaction

