# 1. Architecture

## Client
- Stores surveys locally in SQLite
- Every local change is written immediately to local DB
- Changes are also appended to a `sync_queue`
- When network returns:
  - app sends queued changes to server
  - server applies them
  - app fetches latest remote changes
  - app marks queue items as synced

## Server
- Stores canonical survey records
- Accepts batched changes
- Returns:
  - applied changes
  - conflicts if any
  - latest server changes since last sync timestamp

