# Example: better queue-based sync design

If you want a more robust architecture, here is a queue-table approach.

## Queue insert in `db.js`

```javascript
export const initDB = () => {
  db.transaction(tx => {
    tx.executeSql(`
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS surveys (
        id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
        title TEXT NOT NULL,
        location TEXT,
        notes TEXT,
        createdAt TEXT NOT NULL,
        synced INTEGER NOT NULL
      );
    `);

    tx.executeSql(`
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sync_queue (
        id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
        entityType TEXT NOT NULL,
        entityId TEXT NOT NULL,
        action TEXT NOT NULL,
        payload TEXT NOT NULL,
        createdAt TEXT NOT NULL,
        attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
      );
    `);
  });
};
```

## Add queue item when saving survey

```javascript
export const addToSyncQueue = (item) => {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    db.transaction(tx => {
      tx.executeSql(
        `INSERT INTO sync_queue (id, entityType, entityId, action, payload, createdAt, attempts)
         VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?);`,
        [
          item.id,
          item.entityType,
          item.entityId,
          item.action,
          JSON.stringify(item.payload),
          item.createdAt,
          item.attempts || 0
        ],
        (_, result) => resolve(result),
        (_, error) => {
          reject(error);
          return false;
        }
      );
    });
  });
};
```

## Process queue

```javascript
export const getQueueItems = () => {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    db.transaction(tx => {
      tx.executeSql(
        `SELECT * FROM sync_queue ORDER BY datetime(createdAt) ASC;`,
        [],
        (_, result) => resolve(result.rows._array),
        (_, error) => {
          reject(error);
          return false;
        }
      );
    });
  });
};

export const removeQueueItem = (id) => {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    db.transaction(tx => {
      tx.executeSql(
        `DELETE FROM sync_queue WHERE id = ?;`,
        [id],
        (_, result) => resolve(result),
        (_, error) => {
          reject(error);
          return false;
        }
      );
    });
  });
};
```

Then sync by processing queue items instead of directly scanning `surveys`.

