# Important improvement: retry failed items

Right now failed outbox items are marked `failed` and won’t retry automatically. For a real app, use retry counts and keep them pending unless permanently invalid.

Here is a better outbox strategy.

## Improved `addToOutbox`

```javascript
export async function addToOutbox(action) {
  const db = await dbPromise;
  return db.add(OUTBOX_STORE, {
    ...action,
    status: 'pending',
    retryCount: 0,
    createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  });
}
```

## Replace failure handler

```javascript
export async function rescheduleOutboxItem(id, error) {
  const db = await dbPromise;
  const item = await db.get(OUTBOX_STORE, id);
  if (!item) return;

  item.retryCount = (item.retryCount || 0) + 1;
  item.lastError = error;
  item.lastTriedAt = new Date().toISOString();

  if (item.retryCount >= 5) {
    item.status = 'failed';
  } else {
    item.status = 'pending';
  }

  await db.put(OUTBOX_STORE, item);
}
```

## Use in sync loop

```javascript
import { rescheduleOutboxItem } from './db';
```

Then:

```javascript
catch (err) {
  console.error('Sync failed for outbox item', item.id, err);
  await rescheduleOutboxItem(item.id, err.message);
}
```

