# 15. Suggested backend API contract

A backend that works well for offline sync usually supports:

## Create
```http
POST /surveys
Content-Type: application/json
```

## Update
```http
PUT /surveys/:id
Content-Type: application/json
```

## Delete
```http
DELETE /surveys/:id
```

## Pull changes since timestamp
Better than fetching all surveys every time:

```http
GET /surveys?updatedSince=2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
```

This is much more scalable.

