## Replacing simulated updates with real market data

You can swap the `updatePrices()` simulation with a WebSocket feed.

Example:

```js
const socket = new WebSocket("wss://your-stock-feed.example.com");

socket.onmessage = (event) => {
  const update = JSON.parse(event.data);
  // update = { symbol: "AAPL", price: 193.42, volume: 1234567 }

  data = data.map(stock => {
    if (stock.symbol !== update.symbol) return stock;

    const changePct = ((update.price - stock.prevClose) / stock.prevClose) * 100;

    return {
      ...stock,
      price: update.price,
      volume: update.volume ?? stock.volume,
      changePct: +changePct.toFixed(2)
    };
  });

  render();
};
```

