## Example: replacing simulated updates with real WebSocket

You could adapt `pushTick()` into something like:

```js
const socket = new WebSocket('wss://your-stock-feed');

socket.onmessage = (event) => {
  const tick = JSON.parse(event.data);
  // tick = { symbol: 'AAPL', price: 192.34, timestamp: 1712345678901 }

  const row = heatmap.symbols.indexOf(tick.symbol);
  if (row === -1) return;

  const series = heatmap.data[row];
  const changePct =
    ((tick.price - heatmap.basePrices[tick.symbol]) / heatmap.basePrices[tick.symbol]) * 100;

  series.push({
    timestamp: tick.timestamp,
    price: tick.price,
    changePct
  });

  if (series.length > heatmap.timeSteps) {
    series.shift();
  }

  heatmap.render();
};
```

