# How to make this more production-grade

## 1. Replace channels with lock-free ring buffers
For lower latency:
- Disruptor-style ring buffer
- Shared memory queues
- Single producer / single consumer queues where possible

## 2. Use binary protocols
Avoid JSON in hot path.
Use:
- FlatBuffers
- Cap’n Proto
- custom packed structs
- or no serialization at all in-process

## 3. Use fixed-point math only
Never use floating-point for money.

## 4. Add proper order lifecycle
Support:
- New
- Ack
- Partial fill
- Fill
- Cancel
- Cancel reject
- Replace
- Reject

## 5. Add persistence
At minimum:
- append-only event log
- execution reports
- risk decisions
- order state snapshots

## 6. Add observability
- p50/p99 latency per stage
- dropped message counters
- queue depth
- order reject reasons
- exchange round-trip time

## 7. Add replay
Store market data and execution events so you can:
- replay bugs
- backtest strategies on real event streams
- validate deterministic behavior

