# Design principles for low latency and scalability

## For low latency
- Preallocate memory where possible
- Avoid unnecessary heap allocations
- Minimize locks on the hot path
- Use bounded queues / ring buffers
- Keep messages small and cache-friendly
- Separate hot path from slow path
- Use binary protocols internally if needed

## For scalability
- Make components independently deployable
- Define stable internal event schemas
- Separate exchange adapters from business logic
- Support replay from event logs
- Make state reconstruction deterministic
- Partition by symbol/account/venue where appropriate

