# 6. In-process event bus

For low latency, start with an in-memory bus. Later you can replace this with NATS, Kafka, Aeron, Redis Streams, or a custom UDP/TCP transport.

## `src/bus.rs`

```rust
use crossbeam::channel::{unbounded, Receiver, Sender};
use crate::types::Event;

#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct EventBus {
    tx: Sender<Event>,
}

impl EventBus {
    pub fn new() -> (Self, Receiver<Event>) {
        let (tx, rx) = unbounded();
        (Self { tx }, rx)
    }

    pub fn publish(&self, event: Event) {
        let _ = self.tx.send(event);
    }

    pub fn publisher(&self) -> Sender<Event> {
        self.tx.clone()
    }
}
```

