# 14. Why this is scalable

This skeleton scales because each concern is isolated:

- `strategy.rs` can become multiple strategies
- `execution.rs` can become one adapter per exchange
- `risk.rs` can become a layered pre-trade risk service
- `oms.rs` can evolve into a durable state machine
- `bus.rs` can be swapped from in-process to distributed transport

You can later split the monolith into services like this:

```text
[Market Data Service] ---> [Message Bus] ---> [Strategy Service]
                                            ---> [Risk Service]
                                            ---> [OMS]
                                            ---> [Analytics]

[Strategy Service] ---> [Risk Service] ---> [Execution Gateway] ---> [Exchange]
```

