# 6. Low-latency queue abstraction

This lets you swap implementations later.

## `EventQueue.java`

```java
package com.yourorg.trading.infra;

public interface EventQueue<T> {
    boolean offer(T event);
    T poll();
}
```

## `SpscRingBuffer.java`

A simple single-producer/single-consumer ring buffer.

```java
package com.yourorg.trading.infra;

import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;

public final class SpscRingBuffer<T> implements EventQueue<T> {
    private final Object[] buffer;
    private final int mask;
    private final AtomicLong head = new AtomicLong(0);
    private final AtomicLong tail = new AtomicLong(0);

    public SpscRingBuffer(int capacityPowerOfTwo) {
        if (Integer.bitCount(capacityPowerOfTwo) != 1) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Capacity must be power of two");
        }
        this.buffer = new Object[capacityPowerOfTwo];
        this.mask = capacityPowerOfTwo - 1;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean offer(T event) {
        long currentTail = tail.get();
        long wrapPoint = currentTail - buffer.length;
        if (head.get() <= wrapPoint) {
            return false;
        }
        buffer[(int) (currentTail & mask)] = event;
        tail.lazySet(currentTail + 1);
        return true;
    }

    @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
    @Override
    public T poll() {
        long currentHead = head.get();
        if (currentHead >= tail.get()) {
            return null;
        }
        int index = (int) (currentHead & mask);
        Object event = buffer[index];
        buffer[index] = null;
        head.lazySet(currentHead + 1);
        return (T) event;
    }
}
```

