# 16. Better low-latency version of the event model

If you want to reduce allocations, don’t pass generic `Object payload`. Use mutable preallocated event slots.

Example:

```java
package com.yourorg.trading.common.event;

import com.yourorg.trading.common.model.ExecutionReport;
import com.yourorg.trading.common.model.MarketDataTick;
import com.yourorg.trading.common.model.OrderRequest;

public final class MutableEvent {
    public EventType type;
    public MarketDataTick marketDataTick;
    public OrderRequest orderRequest;
    public ExecutionReport executionReport;

    public void clear() {
        type = null;
        marketDataTick = null;
        orderRequest = null;
        executionReport = null;
    }
}
```

This is closer to how high-performance event loops are often structured.

