## B. Avoid `println!` in hot path
Use:
- lock-free metrics counters
- async logging on side channel

## C. Better time handling
Use:
- invariant TSC or hardware timestamps if available
- PTP synchronization

## D. Better persistence
Use:
- binary event journal
- batched writes
- memory-mapped files
- replay support

## E. Better risk engine
Add:
- notional limits
- order rate limits
- fat-finger checks
- self-trade prevention
- per-strategy and global kill switches

## F. Better OMS
Add:
- cancel/replace support
- idempotency
- reconciliation
- recovery from exchange session resets

## G. Better execution gateway
Add:
- real exchange protocol adapters
- FIX/OUCH/ITCH/native binary support
- session heartbeat/reconnect logic
- sequence number handling

## H. CPU and OS tuning
For actual low latency:
- CPU pinning
- isolated cores
- NUMA awareness
- huge pages
- NIC tuning
- kernel bypass where needed (DPDK, Solarflare/OpenOnload, etc.)

