# 1. Architecture

## Initial design goals
- **Low latency**
  - in-memory processing
  - bounded channels
  - minimal allocations where practical
- **Scalable later**
  - clean service boundaries
  - message-driven internal APIs
  - shared protocol types
- **Safe initial implementation**
  - Rust ownership/thread safety
  - explicit sequencing
- **Extensible**
  - risk checks
  - persistence/journaling
  - replication
  - multiple instruments
  - sharded matching engines

## Initial topology
```text
Client TCP
   |
   v
[ Gateway ]
   |
   v
[ Order Manager ] ---> [ Risk checks later ]
   |
   v
[ Matching Engine ]
   |
   +----> [ Market Data Publisher ]
   |
   +----> [ Execution Reports back to Gateway ]
```

For the first version, these can run in one process with separate async tasks/threads. Later, they can be split into separate processes or hosts.

