# Why this is a good initial implementation

## 1. Event-driven core
The system is centered around typed events, which makes it easy to:

- add new strategies
- add persistence
- add monitoring
- replay events in backtests/simulations

## 2. Modular boundaries
Even though it runs in one process, the boundaries are already there:

- market data
- strategy
- risk
- execution

This makes future extraction straightforward.

## 3. Low-latency-friendly
This is not HFT-grade yet, but it is heading in the right direction:

- no heavy database in hot path
- in-memory processing
- bounded channels
- async runtime
- minimal allocations in core flow can be optimized later

## 4. Easy to scale
Later, you can replace the in-process bus with:

- lock-free ring buffers
- Aeron
- Redis streams for non-hot-path
- Kafka for analytics/audit only

