# 4. Why this is fast

This implementation uses several performance-friendly patterns:

## Sharded worker model
Instead of one giant lock around processing, messages are distributed across workers.

## Bounded queues
Prevents unbounded memory growth and gives you **backpressure**.

## Batch draining
Workers process messages in batches, reducing queue overhead.

## Atomic counters
Very cheap throughput accounting.

## Histogram-based latency tracking
You get p50/p95/p99/p999 instead of just averages.

