# 7. Example: per-worker latency histograms

If you want lower contention, here’s a better worker metrics pattern:

```rust
struct WorkerStats {
    processed: AtomicU64,
    hist: Mutex<Histogram<u64>>,
}

fn worker_loop(
    rx: Receiver<Message>,
    stats: Arc<WorkerStats>,
) {
    loop {
        match rx.recv() {
            Ok(msg) => {
                let latency = now_nanos().saturating_sub(msg.ingress_ts_nanos);
                stats.processed.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
                if let Ok(mut h) = stats.hist.lock() {
                    let _ = h.record(latency);
                }
            }
            Err(_) => break,
        }
    }
}
```

Then merge histograms in the metrics thread.

