# Optional: batch-draining worker optimization

You can replace the worker loop with a small batching strategy:

```rust
async fn worker_loop(self: Arc<Self>, _worker_id: usize, rx: Receiver<Message>) {
    let mut batch = Vec::with_capacity(1024);

    while self.running.load(Ordering::Relaxed) {
        match rx.recv_async().await {
            Ok(first) => {
                batch.push(first);

                while let Ok(msg) = rx.try_recv() {
                    batch.push(msg);
                    if batch.len() >= 1024 {
                        break;
                    }
                }

                for msg in batch.drain(..) {
                    self.route_message(msg);
                }
            }
            Err(_) => break,
        }
    }
}
```

This often improves throughput significantly.

