## Optional: faster delimiter scanning

The loop:

```rust
for i in 0..chunk.len() {
    if chunk[i] == b'\n' {
        ...
    }
}
```

is simple and often quite fast, but for even higher throughput you can use:
- `memchr` crate for optimized byte search
- SIMD scanning

Here is a `memchr`-based variant for the inner scan:

```rust
use memchr::memchr_iter;

pub fn parse_with_memchr<R: Read, F>(
    reader: &mut R,
    chunk_size: usize,
    mut on_record: F,
) -> io::Result<u64>
where
    F: FnMut(&[u8]) -> io::Result<()>,
{
    let mut buf = vec![0u8; chunk_size];
    let mut carry = Vec::with_capacity(1024);
    let mut total_records = 0u64;

    loop {
        let n = reader.read(&mut buf)?;
        if n == 0 {
            break;
        }

        let chunk = &buf[..n];
        let mut start = 0;

        for i in memchr_iter(b'\n', chunk) {
            let line = &chunk[start..i];

            if carry.is_empty() {
                on_record(trim_cr(line))?;
            } else {
                carry.extend_from_slice(line);
                on_record(trim_cr(&carry))?;
                carry.clear();
            }

            total_records += 1;
            start = i + 1;
        }

        if start < chunk.len() {
            carry.extend_from_slice(&chunk[start..]);
        }
    }

    if !carry.is_empty() {
        on_record(trim_cr(&carry))?;
        total_records += 1;
    }

    Ok(total_records)
}
```

