# Parsing structured fields without allocation

If each line contains delimited fields, parse them in-place.

Example: comma-separated fields

```cpp
#include <array>
#include <optional>

struct ParsedRow {
    std::string_view col1;
    std::string_view col2;
    std::string_view col3;
};

std::optional<ParsedRow> parse_csv3(std::string_view line) {
    size_t p1 = line.find(',');
    if (p1 == std::string_view::npos) return std::nullopt;

    size_t p2 = line.find(',', p1 + 1);
    if (p2 == std::string_view::npos) return std::nullopt;

    ParsedRow row{
        line.substr(0, p1),
        line.substr(p1 + 1, p2 - p1 - 1),
        line.substr(p2 + 1)
    };
    return row;
}
```

Usage:

```cpp
parser.parse(input, [&](std::string_view line) {
    auto row = parse_csv3(line);
    if (!row) return;

    // Process fields directly from string_view
    // No copies unless you explicitly make them
});
```

