## Why this is memory-efficient

### 1. Fixed reusable buffer
The parser uses one reusable byte buffer and only grows it if a single record exceeds buffer capacity.

### 2. No full-file loading
It processes data incrementally, so memory usage stays roughly constant even for multi-GB input.

### 3. Callback-based processing
Each record is handled immediately. You don’t accumulate parsed records in RAM.

### 4. Byte-slice parsing
The parser works on `&[u8]` rather than allocating `String`s for every line.

