# If you need structured parsing

If each line contains fields like:

```text
timestamp,user_id,event_type,value
```

you can parse fields without allocating a `Vec<&[u8]>` by scanning in place:

```rust
fn parse_csv_like_line(line: &[u8]) -> Option<(&[u8], &[u8], &[u8], &[u8])> {
    let mut parts = [0usize; 3];
    let mut found = 0;

    for (i, &b) in line.iter().enumerate() {
        if b == b',' {
            if found < 3 {
                parts[found] = i;
                found += 1;
            } else {
                return None;
            }
        }
    }

    if found != 3 {
        return None;
    }

    let a = &line[..parts[0]];
    let b = &line[parts[0] + 1..parts[1]];
    let c = &line[parts[1] + 1..parts[2]];
    let d = &line[parts[2] + 1..];

    Some((a, b, c, d))
}
```

