- Zero-copy-ish parsing within a reusable buffer
- Incremental consumption without loading the whole file
- Minimal allocations
- Support for records split across buffer boundaries
- A callback-based processing model so parsed records can be handled immediately

This example parses newline-delimited records, with fields separated by commas. It is intended as a strong starting point, not a fully specialized production parser.

