## Why this is efficient

### 1. Fixed-size buffer
The parser reads into a reusable fixed-size buffer, so memory usage stays bounded regardless of file size.

### 2. Zero-copy fast path
If a record is fully contained in the current chunk, it passes a slice directly to the handler without copying.

### 3. Boundary-safe carry buffer
Only incomplete records are copied into `carry`, which is necessary when a record spans chunks.

### 4. Streaming callback model
Records are processed immediately via `RecordHandler`, avoiding accumulation of parsed output in memory.

