# Why this is memory-efficient

## 1. Streaming input
It reads from `Read` incrementally rather than loading the entire file.

## 2. Reused buffer
The parser maintains one reusable internal byte buffer.

## 3. Compaction instead of accumulation
Unconsumed bytes are shifted to the front when needed, avoiding unbounded growth in normal cases.

## 4. Per-record allocation only
Only the current record is copied into `Record.data`, so memory stays proportional to:
- buffer size
- current record size
- current field metadata

not total file size.

