## A more optimized variant using `memchr`

If you want a slightly faster version, replace byte-by-byte scans with `memchr`.

Add dependency:

```toml
[dependencies]
memchr = "2"
```

Then update scanning logic:

```rust
use memchr::memchr;

fn next_line(&mut self) -> io::Result<Option<&[u8]>> {
    loop {
        if let Some(rel_pos) = memchr(b'\n', &self.buf[self.start..self.end]) {
            let line_end = self.start + rel_pos;
            let mut line = &self.buf[self.start..line_end];
            if let Some(b'\r') = line.last().copied() {
                line = &line[..line.len() - 1];
            }
            self.start = line_end + 1;
            return Ok(Some(line));
        }

        if self.eof {
            if self.start < self.end {
                let mut line = &self.buf[self.start..self.end];
                if let Some(b'\r') = line.last().copied() {
                    line = &line[..line.len() - 1];
                }
                self.start = self.end;
                return Ok(Some(line));
            } else {
                return Ok(None);
            }
        }

        self.fill_buf()?;
    }
}
```

And similarly for field splitting.

