# If you want stricter memory limits

You can add startup resource limits like:

```c
#include <sys/resource.h>

static int apply_memory_limits(void) {
    struct rlimit rl;

    rl.rlim_cur = 8 * 1024 * 1024;
    rl.rlim_max = 8 * 1024 * 1024;
    if (setrlimit(RLIMIT_AS, &rl) < 0) return -1;

    rl.rlim_cur = 1 * 1024 * 1024;
    rl.rlim_max = 1 * 1024 * 1024;
    if (setrlimit(RLIMIT_STACK, &rl) < 0) return -1;

    return 0;
}
```

Then call it early in `main()`.

Note: `RLIMIT_AS` behavior varies somewhat by platform and libc usage.

