## Optional strict memory limit

If you want, you can add an address-space limit at startup:

```c
#include <sys/resource.h>

static int set_mem_limit_bytes(rlim_t bytes) {
    struct rlimit rl;
    rl.rlim_cur = bytes;
    rl.rlim_max = bytes;
    return setrlimit(RLIMIT_AS, &rl);
}
```

Then call, for example:

```c
set_mem_limit_bytes(8 * 1024 * 1024);
```

You could also use `RLIMIT_DATA` on some systems, though behavior varies.

