## Notes on strict memory limits

This program sets:
- `RLIMIT_AS` — total virtual memory
- `RLIMIT_DATA` — data segment size

This is helpful, but note:
- shared libraries and libc still consume memory
- very tiny limits may prevent startup
- stack is not directly capped here; you could also add `RLIMIT_STACK`

If you want even tighter control, add:

```c
if (setrlimit(RLIMIT_STACK, &rl) != 0) {
    perror("setrlimit(RLIMIT_STACK)");
    return -1;
}
```

But then ensure your stack usage remains very small.

