# Performance notes

To make it more “high-performance” in production:

- avoid refreshing all process data every tick if not needed
- separate fast and slow sampling intervals:
  - CPU/memory every 1–5s
  - disk every 30–60s
  - process inventory every 10–30s
- use bounded async channels if you split collector/enforcer/logger tasks
- export metrics to Prometheus instead of logging everything
- batch logs and reduce per-process logging under pressure
- pin policy checks to only the metrics you care about

