Below is an initial, performance-oriented implementation of a network flow analyzer intended for gigabit-scale traffic. It is written in Rust for speed and memory safety, uses packet capture via `pcap`, tracks basic 5-tuple flows, and exports periodic statistics.

This is an MVP focused on:
- High-throughput packet ingestion
- Efficient in-memory flow aggregation
- Periodic expiration/export
