## Notes on performance
This is minimal and functional, but not yet optimized for true sustained gigabit+ monitoring under worst-case packet rates. To move toward that safely in a lab setting, focus on:

- preallocating larger flow tables
- sharding flow maps per CPU/core
- using lock-free queues between capture and aggregation threads
- batching packet processing
- using AF_PACKET/TPACKETv3, XDP, DPDK, or PF_RING where appropriate
- avoiding heap allocations in the hot path
- using flow expiration wheels instead of full-map scans
- exporting summaries instead of raw packet payloads

