# Example: simpler IIR filter instead of moving average

If you prefer a cheaper filter computationally:

```c
float IIR_Filter(float input)
{
    static bool initialized = false;
    static float y = 0.0f;
    const float alpha = 0.2f;

    if (!initialized)
    {
        y = input;
        initialized = true;
    }
    else
    {
        y = alpha * input + (1.0f - alpha) * y;
    }

    return y;
}
```

You could use this in `Sensor_ReadAndProcess()` instead of the moving average.

