# 5. How the Processing Works

## Analog sensor
- Reads raw ADC counts
- Converts to voltage:
  \[
  V = \frac{raw}{4095} \times 3.3
  \]

- Applies low-pass filter:
  \[
  y[n] = \alpha x[n] + (1-\alpha) y[n-1]
  \]

This reduces noise and gives a more stable value.

## Temperature sensor
- Reads temperature in °C
- Applies same low-pass filter
- Triggers alert if filtered temperature exceeds threshold

