# Optional Improved Processing Example

If you want a lighter filter than a moving average, use an **exponential filter**:

```c
static float Sensor_ExpFilter(float input)
{
    static bool initialized = false;
    static float filtered = 0.0f;
    const float alpha = 0.2f;   // 0..1, lower = smoother

    if (!initialized)
    {
        filtered = input;
        initialized = true;
    }
    else
    {
        filtered = alpha * input + (1.0f - alpha) * filtered;
    }

    return filtered;
}
```

This is often better for small MCUs because it uses less RAM and CPU.

