## More embedded-friendly fixed-point version

If you want to avoid floating point, you can:

- represent acceleration in milli-g
- use integer LPF:
  - `y += ((x - y) * alpha_num) / alpha_den`
- approximate magnitude with:
  - `|ax| + |ay| + |az|`
  - or `max + 0.5*(mid + min)` style approximation

Example magnitude approximation:

```c
static inline int32_t abs_i32(int32_t x) { return x < 0 ? -x : x; }

static inline int32_t approx_mag(int32_t ax, int32_t ay, int32_t az) {
    int32_t x = abs_i32(ax);
    int32_t y = abs_i32(ay);
    int32_t z = abs_i32(az);

    int32_t max = x;
    int32_t mid = y;
    int32_t min = z;

    if (max < mid) { int32_t t = max; max = mid; mid = t; }
    if (mid < min) { int32_t t = mid; mid = min; min = t; }
    if (max < mid) { int32_t t = max; max = mid; mid = t; }

    return max + ((mid + min) >> 2); // cheap approximation
}
```

