Below is a compact embedded-style C implementation of an accelerometer anomaly-detection pipeline suitable for a microcontroller.

It includes:
- DC offset removal with a simple high-pass filter
- Magnitude estimation
- Moving average baseline
- Variance-based noise estimate
- Z-score style anomaly detection
- Spike and sustained anomaly detection
- Fixed-size memory, no dynamic allocation

You can adapt it to raw I2C/SPI accelerometer samples.

