# How it works

## 1. Bias removal
Accelerometers often have offset error. We subtract configured bias:

```c
x = raw.x - bias_x;
```

## 2. Low-pass filter
A first-order IIR filter reduces noise:

```c
filt_x += alpha * (x - filt_x);
```

## 3. Magnitude
We reduce 3-axis data to one scalar:

```c
mag = sqrt(x² + y² + z²)
```

This is orientation-independent enough for many simple anomaly tasks.

## 4. Rolling baseline
We keep an exponentially weighted moving mean and variance of magnitude.

## 5. Anomaly score
We compute a normalized deviation:

```c
score = abs(mag - mean) / stddev
```

## 6. Debounce
One noisy sample should not trigger an alert, so require multiple consecutive threshold crossings.

