## Lower-memory alternative: exponential filter

If RAM is very tight, replace the moving average with an IIR filter:

```c
typedef struct {
    uint16_t value;
    bool initialized;
} ExpFilter;

static uint16_t exp_filter_update(ExpFilter *f, uint16_t sample) {
    /* alpha = 1/8 */
    if (!f->initialized) {
        f->value = sample;
        f->initialized = true;
    } else {
        f->value = (uint16_t)((7U * f->value + sample) / 8U);
    }
    return f->value;
}
```

This uses much less memory than a moving average.

