## Smaller alternative: exponential moving average

If RAM is very tight, use an EMA instead of a ring buffer.

```c
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stdbool.h>

#define EMA_SHIFT  3  // alpha = 1/8

typedef struct {
    uint32_t filtered;   // scaled integer state
    bool initialized;
} EmaFilter;

static void ema_init(EmaFilter *f, uint16_t sample) {
    f->filtered = ((uint32_t)sample << EMA_SHIFT);
    f->initialized = true;
}

static uint16_t ema_update(EmaFilter *f, uint16_t sample) {
    uint32_t target = ((uint32_t)sample << EMA_SHIFT);
    f->filtered += (target - f->filtered) >> EMA_SHIFT;
    return (uint16_t)(f->filtered >> EMA_SHIFT);
}
```

This version:
- uses much less RAM
- is very cheap computationally
- works well for noisy sensors

