## 3. Suggested improvements for production use

### A. Replace floating point if needed
On very small MCUs, float may be expensive. Consider fixed-point integers:

```c
/* Example: store temperature in tenths of a degree */
int16_t temp_tenths = 753; /* 75.3 C */
```

Benefits:

- faster on MCUs without FPU
- lower code size
- more deterministic

---

### B. Add sensor validity checks
Detect:

- out-of-range values
- stuck sensors
- missing updates
- CRC / bus errors

Example:

```c
static bool sensor_value_valid(sensor_id_t id, float v) {
    switch (id) {
        case SENSOR_TEMP:     return (v >= -40.0f && v <= 125.0f);
        case SENSOR_HUMIDITY: return (v >= 0.0f && v <= 100.0f);
        case SENSOR_PRESSURE: return (v >= 800.0f && v <= 1200.0f);
        default:              return false;
    }
}
```

---

### C. Add hysteresis
To prevent actuator chatter, use separate ON/OFF thresholds.

Example:

- fan ON above 75
- fan OFF below 72

This is better than a single threshold.

---

### D. Separate scheduler/timing
In a real edge node, split tasks by rate:

- sensor sampling every 100 ms
- control loop every 200 ms
- telemetry every 1 s
- diagnostics every 5 s

---

### E. Add command/telemetry interface
For practical deployment, expose:

- current sensor values
- actuator states
- fault flags
- configurable thresholds

Possible interfaces:

- UART
- Modbus RTU
- CAN
- MQTT via gateway
- shared memory / local socket on Linux

