# Even smaller alternative filter

If you want a more memory-efficient version, here is a tiny IIR filter:

```c
typedef struct {
    int16_t value;
    bool initialized;
} IIRFilter;

static void iir_init(IIRFilter *f) {
    f->value = 0;
    f->initialized = false;
}

static int16_t iir_update(IIRFilter *f, int16_t sample) {
    if (!f->initialized) {
        f->value = sample;
        f->initialized = true;
    } else {
        /* alpha = 1/8 */
        f->value = f->value + ((sample - f->value) >> 3);
    }
    return f->value;
}
```

This is often better for very small MCUs.

