## Optional lower-memory filter alternative

If memory is extremely tight, replace the moving average with an exponential moving average:

```c
typedef struct {
    int16_t filtered;
    bool initialized;
    bool valid;
} EmaFilterState;

static void ema_update(EmaFilterState *f, int16_t sample, bool valid) {
    /* alpha = 1/4 */
    if (!valid) {
        f->valid = false;
        return;
    }

    if (!f->initialized) {
        f->filtered = sample;
        f->initialized = true;
    } else {
        f->filtered = (int16_t)((3 * f->filtered + sample) / 4);
    }

    f->valid = true;
}
```

This uses less RAM than a windowed average.

