# 1. Architecture

## Goals
- low memory usage
- predictable behavior
- simple scheduling loop
- no heavy dependencies
- easy to port

## Components
- **Sensor**: produces raw readings
- **Filter**: moving average / threshold filtering
- **Controller**: decides actuator state from filtered values
- **Actuator manager**: applies commands only on state changes
- **Main loop**: periodic execution

## Example behavior
- Temperature sensor sampled every cycle
- Filter smooths readings
- If filtered temperature exceeds threshold, fan turns on
- If it drops below threshold minus hysteresis, fan turns off

This hysteresis avoids actuator chatter.

