# 7. Minimal extension example: integer EMA filter

If you want an even cheaper filter than moving average, replace the filter with EMA:

```c
typedef struct {
    const char *name;
    int32_t raw_value;
    int32_t filtered_value;
    bool initialized;
} sensor_t;

static void sensor_filter_init(sensor_t *s, const char *name) {
    memset(s, 0, sizeof(*s));
    s->name = name;
}

static int32_t sensor_filter_update(sensor_t *s, int32_t new_value) {
    s->raw_value = new_value;

    if (!s->initialized) {
        s->filtered_value = new_value;
        s->initialized = true;
    } else {
        s->filtered_value = s->filtered_value + ((new_value - s->filtered_value) >> 2);
    }

    return s->filtered_value;
}
```

This reduces RAM because it removes the filter window buffer.

