# 11. Better fixed-timestep version

A real physics plugin should usually avoid stepping directly with raw frame delta. Here’s a better subsystem tick model:

```cpp
class FPhysicsSubsystem
{
public:
    void Tick(float DeltaTime)
    {
        if (!bInitialized || !World)
        {
            return;
        }

        Accumulator += DeltaTime;

        constexpr float FixedTimeStep = 1.0f / 60.0f;
        constexpr int MaxStepsPerFrame = 4;

        int Steps = 0;
        while (Accumulator >= FixedTimeStep && Steps < MaxStepsPerFrame)
        {
            World->StepSimulation(FixedTimeStep);
            Accumulator -= FixedTimeStep;
            ++Steps;
        }
    }

private:
    std::unique_ptr<FPhysicsWorld> World;
    bool bInitialized = false;
    float Accumulator = 0.0f;
};
```

This is strongly recommended even in an early version.

