# 12. Better timestep recommendation

Instead of stepping directly with variable `DeltaTime`, use a fixed timestep accumulator:

```cpp
class PhysicsSubsystem
{
public:
    void Tick(float DeltaTime)
    {
        if (!bInitialized || !MainWorld)
        {
            return;
        }

        Accumulator += DeltaTime;
        constexpr float FixedStep = 1.0f / 60.0f;

        while (Accumulator >= FixedStep)
        {
            MainWorld->StepSimulation(FixedStep);
            Accumulator -= FixedStep;
        }
    }

private:
    std::unique_ptr<PhysicsWorld> MainWorld;
    bool bInitialized = false;
    float Accumulator = 0.0f;
};
```

This is usually a much better starting point for physics.

