# 13. Optional improved architecture

A more scalable design would use an internal struct:

```cpp
struct FPhysicsBodyState
{
    TWeakObjectPtr<USimplePhysicsBodyComponent> Component;
    FVector Position;
    FVector Velocity;
    FVector Force;
    float Mass;
    float Radius;
    float Restitution;
    bool bUseGravity;
};
```

Then the world simulates `FPhysicsBodyState` objects and syncs them back to components after each step. That is better for:
- performance
- future multithreading
- determinism
- decoupling engine objects from solver logic

