## Why this works

### 1. Fixed timestep physics
Physics is updated at a constant rate:

```js
const FIXED_DT = 1 / 120;
```

This makes simulation behavior more stable and less dependent on rendering speed.

---

### 2. Frame-rate constraint
Rendering is capped to a target FPS:

```js
if (now - lastRenderTime < FRAME_MIN_TIME) return;
```

This prevents rendering from running too fast and wasting CPU.

---

### 3. Real-time loop
The loop uses:

```js
requestAnimationFrame(loop);
```

This synchronizes rendering with the browser display pipeline.

---

### 4. Rigid body dynamics
Each body has:

- linear position/velocity
- angular position/velocity
- mass
- inertia

Integration is done with a simple Euler step:

```js
this.vy += GRAVITY * dt;
this.x += this.vx * dt;
this.y += this.vy * dt;
this.angle += this.angularVelocity * dt;
```

