## Why this performs well

### 1. Async I/O
Tokio uses non-blocking I/O, allowing a small number of threads to handle many connections concurrently.

### 2. Lock-free request counter
The request counter uses `AtomicU64` instead of a mutex, reducing contention.

### 3. Multi-threaded runtime
Tokio’s multi-thread runtime spreads work across CPU cores.

### 4. Minimal per-request work
Handlers are lightweight and avoid blocking operations.

