## Important note about worker threads

This line:

```rust
#[tokio::main(flavor = "multi_thread", worker_threads = 0)]
```

may not be accepted depending on Tokio version/config, because Tokio generally expects a positive worker thread count when explicitly set.

If that happens, replace it with either:

```rust
#[tokio::main(flavor = "multi_thread")]
```

or explicitly:

```rust
#[tokio::main(flavor = "multi_thread", worker_threads = 8)]
```

A safe default is:

```rust
#[tokio::main(flavor = "multi_thread")]
```

So the final recommended attribute is:

```rust
#[tokio::main(flavor = "multi_thread")]
```

